|~ `::invariant`, the kind of an invariant, and the laws declared under
   it.

   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSBLD#fn]. ~|

:invariant
  |~~ An invariant is a query the values of a kind keep: a quote under
      this tag, written by `holds` in the chain that builds the kind or
      the function it guards, as a law is a quote under `::law` that
      `proves` writes, and laid under the name of the refusal of a value
      that breaks it: a kind of
      `(::kind | holds :TooLargeError |~~ Below ten. ~~| ~(lt 10))`
      declared as `:Small` refuses `::Small#12` under
      `::Small/TooLargeError`.

      An invariant guards the value of a kind or a field of its payload,
      and an input or the answer of a function, by the path of its name,
      and runs when the value is built, read or answered, an invariant of
      a kind's value on the payload beneath the tag, so a verb in it that
      keeps its subject's kind runs over no tag, `~(eq (sort))`; the kinds
      of an input are named where it is taken, `| takes :by … ::number`.
      Declared by a name outside a chain, an invariant holds of nothing
      and is refused.
      ::link~(::kind/holds | doc) ::link~(::fn/holds | doc)
      ::link~(::law | doc) ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The condition its values keep, a quote. ~~| ::quote
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ An invariant is a quote, `::invariant~(gt 0)`, which `holds`
            writes in a chain; a quote under another tag gives the quote
            beneath by `payload`.
        ~~|
    | proves :liesUnderItsRefusal
        |~~ The node an invariant of a chain lays under the name of its
            refusal holds a quote under `::invariant`.
        ~~|
        ~(::vec/take/CountNotIntegerError | binding | value | tag | eq ::invariant)
    | proves :readsThePayloadBeneathTheTag
        |~~ An invariant of a kind's value reads the payload beneath the
            tag, so a verb that keeps its subject's kind runs in it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Sorted |~~ In order. ~~| (::kind | holds :NotSortedError |~~ In order. ~~| ~(eq (sort))) | get [~(::Sorted[1 2] | payload) ~(::Sorted[2 1] !| tag)] | eq [[1 2] ::Sorted/NotSortedError])
    | proves :refusesUnderItsName
        |~~ A value that breaks an invariant is refused under its name. ~~|
        ~(:Small |~~ Below ten. ~~| (::kind | holds :TooLargeError |~~ A number below ten. ~~| ~(lt 10)) | get [~(::Small#3 | tag) ~(::Small#12 !| tag)] | eq [::Small ::Small/TooLargeError])
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ An invariant is a quote. ~~|
        ~(::invariant#5 !| tag | eq ::invariant/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :isWrittenInAChain
        |~~ An invariant declared by a name is refused: it is written in a
            chain.
        ~~|
        ~(:Positive ::invariant~(gt 0) !| tag | eq ::bind/WrittenOutsideItsChainError)
    | proves :holdsAQuoteByItsOwnTag
        |~~ The condition of an invariant is a quote, a quote under another
            tag refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::invariant::Foo~(gt 0) !| get [~(tag) ~(found | tag)] | eq [::invariant/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::Foo])

